## Finding

Culprit: `patches/llama/metal/0083-metal-fa-prefill-block-is-off-on-64-lane-cards.patch`, its single hunk in `src/llama-graph.cpp` - `llm_graph_context::build_attn_mha()`, `amd_prefill_fa_blocked`, worktree HEAD `src/llama-graph.cpp:2955` (condition lines 2956-2960).

0083 turned the blocked prefill route off on 64-lane cards unless `TOSH_FA_PF_W64=1`. That flag gates `amd_prefill_decomposed` (`:2983`, used `:2993`) and so `use_flash_attn` (`:2997`). `metal_simd_width` is the D700's probed SIMD width and is non-null at `-ngl 0` too (devices registered, weights on host), so the choice is made for a CPU-only run as well:

- beta.7: decomposed prefill - `MUL_MAT`(KQ) -> `soft_max` -> `MUL_MAT`(AV)
- beta 8: `ggml_flash_attn_ext` (online softmax accumulator)

Same math, different sum order -> divergence at offset 216 (0.6B band1100) and 225 (8B band16) after 1483-token prompt. Legitimate reordering, not a correctness bug - but a graph change driven by GPU measurement, keyed off device SIMD width rather than where the node runs.

Proof: `hunk` build (HEAD, only that condition restored to beta.7 form) = beta.7 text on all 3 cells; `hunk-8b` = beta.7 8B band16 (282 chars); at HEAD with no code change `TOSH_FA_PF_W64=1` also restores beta.7 text (`w64`). Ruled out: 0082, 0086, 0085, and 0084 (Metal-only files; 0083 revert alone already restores beta.7 with 0084 applied).

Determinism: beta.7 engine reproduces beta.7 ref exactly; beta 8 engine reproduces gates-beta8 ref exactly when cells run 16/300/1100 in gate order (`d-all3`). Side observation: band1100 as first request on a cold server gives 271 chars on both engines; refs are warm-sequence.

